s of the Federal Government \nshall be closed on January 9, 2025, as a mark of respect for James Earl \nCarter, Jr., the thirty-ninth President of the United States.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"90 FR 187, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 1","sha256":"bce0d1975ed4eafda1dc82a6528da5a9fbe8065583f3291d92ef05c74a9990f8","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2025-01-03/pdf/2024-31766.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14133#sec1","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 2. The heads of executive departments and agencies may determine \nthat certain offices and installations of their organizations, or parts thereof, \nmust remain open and that certain employees must report for duty on \nJanuary 9, 2025, for reasons of national security, defense, or other public \nneed.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"90 FR 187, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 2","sha256":"bce0d1975ed4eafda1dc82a6528da5a9fbe8065583f3291d92ef05c74a9990f8","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2025-01-03/pdf/2024-31766.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14133#sec2","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 3. January 9, 2025, shall be considered as falling within the scope \nof Executive Order 11582 of February 11, 1971, and of 5 U.S.C. 5546 and \n6103(b) and other similar statutes insofar as they relate to the pay and \nleave of employees of the United States.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"90 FR 187, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 3","sha256":"bce0d1975ed4eafda1dc82a6528da5a9fbe8065583f3291d92ef05c74a9990f8","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2025-01-03/pdf/2024-31766.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14133#sec3","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 4. The Director of the Office of Personnel Management shall take \nsuch actions as may be necessary to implement this order.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"90 FR 187, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 4","sha256":"bce0d1975ed4eafda1dc82a6528da5a9fbe8065583f3291d92ef05c74a9990f8","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2025-01-03/pdf/2024-31766.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14133#sec4","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) Nothing in this order shall be construed \nto impair or otherwise affect: \n(i) the authority granted by law to an executive department or agency, \nor the head thereof; or \n(ii) the functions of the Director of the Office of Management and Budget \nrelating to budgetary, administrative, or legislative proposals.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"90 FR 187, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 5(a)","sha256":"bce0d1975ed4eafda1dc82a6528da5a9fbe8065583f3291d92ef05c74a9990f8","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2025-01-03/pdf/2024-31766.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14133#sec5(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) This order shall be implemented consistent with applicable law and \nsubject to the availability of appropriations. \nVerDate Sep<11>2014 16:47 Jan 02, 2025 Jkt 265001 PO 00000 Frm 00001 Fmt 4790 Sfmt 4790 E:\\FR\\FM\\03JAE0.SGM 03JAE0lotter on DSK11XQN23PROD with FR_PREZDOC1\n=== PDF page 2 of 2 ===\n188 Federal Register / Vol. 90, No. 2 / Friday, January 3, 2025 / Presidential Documents \n(c) This order is not intended to, and does not, create any right or benefit, \nsubstantive or procedural, enforceable at law or in equity by any party \nagainst the United States, its departments, agencies, or entities, its officers, \nemployees, or agents, or any other person.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"90 FR 187, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 5(b)","sha256":"bce0d1975ed4eafda1dc82a6528da5a9fbe8065583f3291d92ef05c74a9990f8","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2025-01-03/pdf/2024-31766.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14133#sec5(b)","state_at_cutoff":null}],"original_representation":{"p